From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] programs: their own names; iexplore kept out of Open with (5967)

Open with, Task Manager and a program's Properties show a program's
FileDescription. Wine's said "Wine Registry Editor", "Wine Task
Manager", "Wine Explorer", "Wine conhost"...; Open with's More apps
listed "Wine Internet Explorer". Windows' own programs give their plain
names. Each program here gives its own; a file that names none is a
"System component" (was "Wine core dll": ntoskrnl.exe). iexplore -- the
old browser kept for programs that start it -- is kept out of Open with
(NoOpenWith), as the applications Windows hides there are.

Gate test/progname-gate.sh.
---
--- a/include/wine/wine_common_ver.rc
+++ b/include/wine/wine_common_ver.rc
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #ifndef WINE_FILEDESCRIPTION_STR
-#define WINE_FILEDESCRIPTION_STR "Wine core dll"
+#define WINE_FILEDESCRIPTION_STR "System component"
 #endif
 
 #ifndef WINE_FILENAME
--- a/programs/conhost/conhost.rc
+++ b/programs/conhost/conhost.rc
@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@
 
